<h3>1. The Microsoft white paper: same model, different harness</h3>
<p>Microsoft Copilot Studio has two harnesses. The Standard harness is one where the maker wires topics, variables and tools one by one. The other is an agent loop: the model plans, picks tools and retries on failure. The loop was taken from GitHub Copilot's coding agent and was called the GitHub Copilot harness until October 28, when Microsoft renamed it the Microsoft Copilot harness and said it would become a shared foundation across its Copilot products. The rename notice said nothing changed in capabilities or billing.</p>
<p>The white paper released with the November 9 blog post reports an internal evaluation (October 2026) that ran both harnesses on the same tasks with the same models. The headline numbers are below.</p>

